"""PUBLIC GRIEVANCE ASSISTANT -- COMPLETE SINGLE-FILE EDITION

Copy this entire file into app.py. No rag.py, storage.py, agents/ or legal
index downloads are required. The existing 1,092 legal chunks and their FAISS
vectors are embedded at the end, with original source/page metadata retained.
Complete additional amended FIA/police/municipal statutes are not included;
upload current legal material through Regulations when needed.

START:    python -m pip install streamlit
          streamlit run app.py
On an existing Streamlit deployment, replace app.py and reboot the app.
Keep your existing private Streamlit Secrets; do not put keys in this file.

OPTIONAL: python -m pip install crewai groq pypdf reportlab faiss-cpu fastembed
These improve orchestration, PDF extraction/rendering and semantic retrieval.
Without them, built-in sequential Groq requests, keyword search, evidence
uploads, English PDF downloads, local templates and submission still work.
Local bill OCR additionally requires an installed Tesseract executable;
consented Groq vision OCR does not require that executable.

PRIVATE CONFIGURATION (Streamlit Settings > Secrets, or environment variables):
GROQ_API_KEY = "your-active-key"
GROQ_MODEL = "openai/gpt-oss-20b"
For sending email, configure RESEND_API_KEY plus SUBMISSION_FROM, or SMTP_HOST,
SMTP_PORT, SMTP_SECURITY, SMTP_USERNAME, SMTP_PASSWORD and SMTP_FROM.
Sending requires review/authorization. Official portal login/CAPTCHA remains
on the official site. Groq organization/project permissions still apply.
Successful Groq model requests are remembered for the same API key in the
private local database. Retries default to an untried model; a generic access
denial is kept distinct from a documented model-specific permission refusal.
Without an app sender, choose Send using my email app; download an unsent
.eml message with the selected attachments, or open your email/webmail draft.
Webmail links require attaching evidence yourself and clicking Send there.

OPTIONAL WORKER: python app.py --scheduler --watch
Optional indexing: python app.py --ingest --input policies --all-collections
The worker needs an always-on host and the same private settings/databases.
Local SQLite files can disappear on ephemeral hosting; download case backups.
"""
